C++ Single Inheritance – Employee and Developer

Description

This C++ program demonstrates single inheritance using two classes: "Employee" and "Developer".

The "Developer" class inherits the "name" property from the "Employee" class and adds its own "language" property.

Classes Used

1. Employee Class

The "Employee" class is the base class.

- "name" stores the employee's name.
- The constructor initializes the employee's name.
- "protected" allows the derived "Developer" class to access "name".

2. Developer Class

The "Developer" class is the derived class of "Employee".

- "language" stores the programming language.
- The constructor initializes the name and programming language.
- "display()" displays the developer's details.

Main Function

In the "main()" function, a "Developer" object is created with:

- Name: "Neha"
- Programming Language: "C++"

The "display()" function is then called to show the details.

Output

Developer: Neha
Language: C++

OOP Concept Used

Single Inheritance

Employee
    ↓
Developer

"Employee" is the base class, while "Developer" is the derived class.
